tial","note":"Bolaños, Chimaltitán, Colotlán, Hostotipaquillo, Huejúcar, Huequilla el Alto, Mezquitic, San Martín de Bolaños, Santa María de los Ángeles, Totatiche and Villa Guerrero."},{"name":"The state of Colima","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the city of Manzanillo by sea, or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport","direct travel via road 200 from that airport to Manzanillo"]},{"name":"The state of Guerrero, including the city of Acapulco","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air"]},{"name":"Within 40km of the Guatemalan border, from the Pacific Coast up to and including the Gracias a Dios crossing","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential"},{"name":"Federal Highway 199 between Rancho Nuevo, outside San Cristóbal de las Casas, and the Chancalá junction outside Palenque","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"The restriction is the highway segment, not the towns at either end."}]},"timing":{"peak":"Dry season Nov-Apr (Dec-Apr optimal weather + best wildlife) - guided day-trip window","shoulder":"Nov and late-Apr edges","green":"Wet May-Oct (lush, fewer crowds, afternoon storms, hurricane overlap) - Tulum fill-the-beds","fill_the_beds":"No in-reserve beds; applies to Tulum pre/post stay - push May-Oct Tulum value + AM tours","source":"https://www.machupicchu.org/sian-kaan-biosphere-reserve-2026-unesco-world-heritage-day-trip-from-tulum.htm","fire_date":"Early-book ~6-8 weeks ahead for Dec-Apr (seats capped); green-season Tulum-stay push May-Oct","event_peaks":"Dec holiday + New Year, Semana Santa compound the capped-seat crunch","booking_lead":"2-4 weeks ahead in high season - DAILY VISITOR LIMITS cap seats (UNESCO biosphere rations access)"},"jewels":[{"name":"Muyil ancient-Maya-canal float","status":"live","tier":"comfort","bookable_category":"guided expedition","source":"https://www.getyourguide.com/tulum-l248/tulum-sian-ka-an-biosphere-reserve-ancient-maya-canals-tour-t671649/","timing":"Dry season Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"boat run + life-vest drift on 1,200-yr-old Maya-dredged canals ·","si":"expedition","blurb":"boat run + life-vest drift on 1,200-yr-old Maya-dredged canals ·","when":"Dry season Nov-Apr","commission":"affiliate ~4-8% (Viator/GYG) / DMC on application","wells":["activities","move"],"wells_basis":"full pass 2026-10-05, additive — text","si_all":["expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"expedition":"primary","tropical":"destination","wildlife":"destination"},"commission_pct_low":4,"commission_pct_high":8,"commission_lane":["DMC","affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"band+lane"},{"name":"Guided lagoon boat expedition","status":"live","tier":"comfort","bookable_category":"guided boat tour","source":"https://www.mexicokantours.com/sian-kaan-adventure","si":"expedition","commission":"guided-tour affiliate / DMC (Mexico Kan Tours)","wells":["activities","move"],"wells_basis":"full pass 2026-10-05, additive — text","si_all":["expedition","tropical"],"shelf_fit":{"expedition":"primary","tropical":"evidenced","wildlife":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC","affiliate","guide"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Kayak + snorkel Campechen lagoon","status":"live","tier":"comfort","bookable_category":"guided kayak/snorkel","source":"https://www.mexicokantours.com/sian-kaan-adventure","si":"expedition","commission":"affiliate/DMC","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["expedition","tropical"],"shelf_fit":{"expedition":"primary","tropical":"evidenced","wildlife":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC","affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Birding day (300+ species)","status":"future","tier":"premier","bookable_category":"specialist nature tour","source":"https://lifeontheroam.com/sian-kaan-biosphere-reserve/","timing":"Dry season Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"wildlife","when":"Dry season Nov-Apr","commission":"on application, small-group premium","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["wildlife"],"shelf_fit":{"expedition":"destination","tropical":"destination","wildlife":"primary"},"commission_lane":[],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"unparsed"},{"name":"Punta Allen coastal / sandbar","status":"future","tier":"comfort","bookable_category":"guided overland/boat","source":"https://www.thoroughlytravel.com/sian-kaan-biosphere-reserve/","timing":"Dry season Nov-Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"tropical","when":"Dry season Nov-Apr","commission":"DMC/guide on application (~4h unpaved road)","wells":["activities","move"],"wells_basis":"full pass 2026-10-05, additive — text","si_all":["tropical"],"shelf_fit":{"expedition":"destination","tropical":"primary","wildlife":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC","guide"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Sian Ka''an?","a":"Remoteness, heat and mosquitoes — not marine hazards or crime. This is a mangrove/wetland reserve, so the mosquito load is high (repellent, cover up, especially dawn/dusk and rainy season), and sun, heat and dehydration are the genuine risks on a long, unpaved-road day. There is no interior infrastructure — carry water and travel with a comms-equipped guide.","source":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mexico","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What is the signature Sian Ka''an experience?","a":"The Muyil canal float. A boat runs you down ancient trade canals hand-dredged by Maya mariners over 1,200 years ago, then you drift downstream in a life vest on the natural current through mangrove lagoons — a natural lazy river. It is best in the calmer morning (fewer bugs), and bundled tours include transport, meals and an expert guide.","source":"getyourguide.com / lifeontheroam.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"expedition","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"q":"What wildlife can I see in Sian Ka''an?","a":"A great deal — the reserve''s four ecosystems host 300+ bird species, 100+ mammals, 1,200 plants and 52 fish species, with a good chance of dolphins on the lagoon runs. Dedicated dawn birding tours are the way to see the most; wildlife is the reserve''s purpose-built anchor, so book a naturalist-guided product rather than a bare boat ride.","source":"lifeontheroam.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"wildlife","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"q":"How do you actually visit Sian Ka''an, and can I stay inside?","a":"As a guided day trip from Tulum — you cannot sleep in the biosphere, as there is no lodging of any kind inside. Access is guided-only with rationed daily visitor limits, so book 2–4 weeks ahead in high season. Note the fixed Muyil boat driver is transport-only; if you want interpretation, book a nature-guide product, not the bare boat fee.","source":"machupicchu.org / roamingaroundtheworld.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"planning","accessed":"2026-07-04"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit Sian Ka''an?","a":"November–April, the dry season, is best — Dec–April brings optimal weather and the best wildlife viewing. Whatever the season, morning tours are calmer with fewer bugs; the May–October wet season is lush and quieter but brings afternoon storms and hurricane overlap (Jun–Nov). Because seats are capped, book earliest for the Dec–April and holiday windows.","source":"machupicchu.org / lifeontheroam.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"planning","accessed":"2026-07-04"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Sian Ka''an Biosphere Reserve: UNESCO Wetlands Tour","meta_description":"Sian Ka''an - UNESCO biosphere south of Tulum: float 1,200-year-old Maya canals, birds and mangroves. Guided-only, remote; how and when to go.","slug":"sian-kaan-mexico","primary_keyword":"Sian Ka''an Biosphere Reserve","long_tail":["Sian Ka''