isory lists each by name."},{"name":"In Jalisco: eleven northern municipalities","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"Bolaños, Chimaltitán, Colotlán, Hostotipaquillo, Huejúcar, Huequilla el Alto, Mezquitic, San Martín de Bolaños, Santa María de los Ángeles, Totatiche and Villa Guerrero."},{"name":"The state of Colima","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the city of Manzanillo by sea, or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport","direct travel via road 200 from that airport to Manzanillo"]},{"name":"The state of Guerrero, including the city of Acapulco","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air"]},{"name":"Within 40km of the Guatemalan border, from the Pacific Coast up to and including the Gracias a Dios crossing","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential"},{"name":"Federal Highway 199 between Rancho Nuevo, outside San Cristóbal de las Casas, and the Chancalá junction outside Palenque","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"The restriction is the highway segment, not the towns at either end."}]},"timing":{"peak":"November–April (dry, whale-watching, winter N-swell surf)","shoulder":"May–June & October","green":"July–September into early October (hot, hurricane/chubasco, summer S-swell)","booking_lead":"3–5+ months for peak boutique inventory (small supply)","off_season_specials":"Green-season summer surf + desert-wellness value; disclose storm risk + insurance","event_peaks":"Christmas/New Year, Semana Santa, whale Jan–Mar, surf winter N-swell Nov–Mar + summer S-swell Jun–Sep","fire_date":"Late summer/early fall for Nov–Apr peak; late spring for green-season surf/wellness"},"jewels":[{"name":"Gallery walk + Hotel California","status":"future","hook":"Pueblo Mágico galleries + the mythic Hotel California","bookable_category":"free stroll / dining","tier":"essential","source":"https://incabotravel.com/uncover-todos-santos-hotel-california-myths-facts-must-visit-spots (Accessed 2