  ('valladolid-mexico', '10S', 'Valladolid', 'Mexico', 'Valladolid Yucatán', 'live', 'verified', 'kyoto', 'Yucatán (Mérida & Chichén Itzá)', '{"expedition","culture","culinary"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["1543 colonial city + Pueblo Magico (2012), ~150 km from both Merida and Cancun; mid-peninsula base","Cenote Zaci in the heart of town (short staircase, park); swimmable, free w/ ~100 MXN restaurant","Cenote Suytun ~5 km E - iconic single light-beam on stone platform ~1-3 PM; ~250 MXN (230 online), 9 AM-5 PM","Cenote Oxman on a working hacienda - deep sinkhole + roots + rope swing + pool; 150 MXN (350 w/ lunch)","Ek Balam ~30 min N - CLIMBABLE 32 m acropolis (unlike Chichen), intricate stucco; ~170 MXN cash only"],"safety":{"emergency":"911","hospital":"basic hospitals in town; nearest full trauma care Merida (~2 hr W, Star Medica/Clinica de Merida) or Cancun (~2 hr E, Hospiten/Amerimed) or air-evac","air_access_verified":"yes - ~2 hr from MID Merida and ~2 hr from CUN Cancun (~150 km from each)","heat":"intense Yucatan sun - visit cenotes/Ek Balam at 9 AM opening; carry water + SPF; heat exhaustion risk at open ruins","cenote":"Zaci/Suytun/Oxman = swim/snorkel, NO lifeguard; life jackets (mandatory posture for non-swimmers/children); shower off sunscreen; slick platforms (Suytun) + rope swing (Oxman) - jump only where directed","dive_spine":"DISTINGUISH swim/snorkel (no cert) vs GUIDED cavern dive (certified cavern guide, light zone) vs CAVE dive (TECHNICAL - full cave cert, overhead, silt-out - FLAG HARD, never blur). Yucatan = world''s longest flooded caves (Ox-Bel-Ha ~269 km)","hyperbaric_no_fly":"nearest chambers on coast ~2+ hr (SSS/DAN Cancun, Playa, Cozumel; SSS Merida ~2 hr W); interior Yucatan has NO adjacent chamber - multi-hour evac for cave/cavern diving; DAN = nearest hospital first; observe no-fly 18-24 hr after multi-day/repetitive dives; carry DAN insurance","malaria":"effectively none i